WEBVTT

00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:16,050
Is there some sort of progression of symptoms when someone has lymphoma and then starts your

00:00:16,050 --> 00:00:21,570
life and supplement program? Do people go through different stages before they're cancer-free?

00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:27,250
How soon will there be changes? It's been two months and I've not really noticed any decrease

00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:34,130
in the intra-abdominal mass. Well three days ago, I started having pain in that area. Is that a sign

00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:42,130
that the immune system is attacking that area? Well, I do have a video and a blog post on good-paid

00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:48,850
bad-paid that will maybe help you discern that. There's no perfect way to discern whether my

00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:55,650
pain is a good-paid or a bad-paid. They say, well, how could there be any good-paid? Well,

00:00:55,650 --> 00:01:00,770
if your immune system is attacking a site, you're going to have an increase in inflammation at that

00:01:01,170 --> 00:01:07,090
site. That's what an uptick of the immune system is. So you get a B bite, the B sting, and you

00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:12,050
have all this inflammation because of the B sting, because your immune system is setting this entire

00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:21,810
immune attack, trying to deal with this inflammatory thing that is pulsating toxins into your system.

00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:29,810
So the same thing, when you're up, trying to uptick your immune system to fight a cancer, you could

00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:37,330
have an increase in inflammation at that site, and have pain because of that. So I don't know

00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:44,690
if that's a good-paid or a bad-paid. So if you're saying that you can feel like you

00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:55,170
are able to adequately examine a mass, whether it's a breast mass or a mass that's from lymphoma,

00:01:55,810 --> 00:02:02,290
and adequately measure the size, and you can say, after two months, it's not changing size.

00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:13,600
Does that mean it's a bad thing? Maybe, maybe not. So remember, when we're trying to kill cancer,

00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:22,000
we're trying to extend someone's life. We're not... I don't... In our mind, we're always thinking,

00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,240
I want this to go away. You have a mass in your breast or you have a mass, you know, in your

00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:35,040
abdominal cavity, and it's lymphoma, or it's a breast cancer. I want this to go away. Of course,

00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:41,760
we all want it to go away, but really, when you think about it, what is cancer? Cancer is rapidly

00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:48,960
replicating cells. If we could stop it rapidly replicating, and our body would just wall it off,

00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:55,120
wouldn't that be just as good? Well, maybe mentally, it would be better for you,

00:02:55,120 --> 00:03:00,960
for me to have it to disappear, and then we don't see it anymore. But realistically,

00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:08,160
when you have a fairly large mass, it's going to be more difficult for the body to remove that

00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:15,280
mass, to break it down, to get it out of your body, to get rid of the cells, and for you to detox it,

00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:22,000
is that it would be for your body to wall it off and have it not grow. Really, we want, you know,

00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:30,880
a mass to stop growing. Of course, I agree. We want it to go away, but we want it to stop growing,

00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:37,680
and as far as how long does it take for that to take place? Well, to be honest, we may have to tweak

00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:43,920
your program and change things to get it moving in that right direction. And then also, honestly,

00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:48,720
it may take months for it, just with the brakes on it, for it to start shrinking. And then,

00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:56,800
thirdly, it may just stop growing and be walled off and never change size. And you live another 40 years

00:03:56,800 --> 00:04:04,400
with this mass of dead cells in your abdominal cavity. That's a possibility, too.

00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:15,280
So, how do we know what is happening with that? The only perfect way to know if a mass that

00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:20,240
has not changed size, let's say it's not getting bigger, it's not getting smaller, it's still the same

00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:27,920
size. And let's say now, instead of being two months out, or two years out, how would we know if this

00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:33,840
is still active cancer or not? The only way to know at that point would be to go in and remove it

00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:40,960
and then do a pathology report on it. So, you cut it in slices and you look at it at a microscope,

00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:47,360
if they're all dead cells. Of course, you're always going to do that because there's danger of that, too.

00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:54,320
I actually had this story multiple times and I had a lung cancer patient who had multiple masses

00:04:54,320 --> 00:05:00,960
in her chest. And she refused to let the surgeon remove him. He was trying to get her to remove him

00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:09,040
I can't remember how long of a time it was. Finally, she was persuaded, this is a surgeon at Mayo,

00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:14,400
that talked her into doing it. He said it was going to be a relatively quick surgery. The surgery took

00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:22,800
like five times longer than he thought because the tumors that he thought was active cancer was

00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:29,840
just walled off dead cells that broke apart. Like the word he used, the surgeon used was he broke

00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:34,880
it broke apart like a puff ball and it made a mess in that person's lungs and it took forever to

00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:43,360
clean it out. So, maybe you should have let sleeping giants lie. You know, I'm not saying that's

00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:48,560
the case we need to measure. We need to look at all sorts of different things. Like I said, with that

00:05:49,120 --> 00:06:01,120
previous question, look at blood work and look at scans and look at subjective findings as well.

00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:06,160
So, feeling great and feeling fantastic. If I still have this mass, it's not getting any bigger,

00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:11,280
but it's concerning because it's not getting any smaller. While you weigh it out with as many

00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:14,720
possible things that you could do to weigh out whether I'm getting better or not.

